(doc
  (title "YX Protocol: Security Architecture")
  (source-format markdown)
  (converted "2026-07-19")
  (para "**Version:** 1.0.0 **Date:** 2026-01-18 **Status:** Normative Specification **Traceability:** Gap 2.1, 2.2, 2.3, 3.4")
  (section
    (heading "Overview")
    (para "The YX protocol implements defense-in-depth security through three independent layers:")
    (item "1. **HMAC Authentication** (Layer 1) - Packet integrity and authenticity")
    (item "2. **Replay Protection** (Layer 2) - Prevents replay attacks")
    (item "3. **Rate Limiting** (Layer 3) - DDoS mitigation")
    (para "Additionally, Protocol 1 provides optional **AES-256-GCM encryption** for payload confidentiality.")
    (para "**Security Philosophy:** Multiple independent security mechanisms provide redundancy. If one layer fails, others still provide protection."))
  (section
    (heading "Security Pipeline")
    (subsection
      (heading "Send Path")
      (code "Application Data
    ↓
[1] Rate Limit Check (per peer)
    ↓ (if limit exceeded: REJECT)
[2] Protocol Encoding (Protocol 0 or Protocol 1)
    ↓
[3] HMAC Computation (GUID + Payload)
    ↓
[4] UDP Send"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Receive Path")
      (code "UDP Receive
    ↓
[1] Packet Parsing (extract HMAC, GUID, Payload)
    ↓
[2] HMAC Validation (constant-time comparison)
    ↓ (if invalid: REJECT + log to /tmp/hmac_failures.log)
[3] Replay Protection Check (nonce cache lookup)
    ↓ (if seen before: REJECT)
[4] Rate Limit Check (per peer sliding window)
    ↓ (if limit exceeded: REJECT)
[5] Protocol Decoding (Protocol 0 or Protocol 1)
    ↓
[6] Application Delivery")
      (para "**Critical Property:** All three security layers (HMAC, replay protection, rate limiting) are independent. Each provides security value even if others are bypassed.")))
  (section
    (heading "Layer 1: HMAC Authentication")
    (subsection
      (heading "Purpose")
      (para "Verify packet integrity and authenticity using shared symmetric key."))
    (subsection
      (heading "Algorithm")
      (item "**Hash Function:** SHA-256")
      (item "**MAC Construction:** HMAC (RFC 2104)")
      (item "**Truncation:** First 16 bytes (128 bits)")
      (item "**Key Size:** 32 bytes (256 bits)"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Input")
      (code "hmac_input = GUID (6 bytes) + Payload (variable)
hmac_output = HMAC-SHA256(hmac_input, key)
hmac_truncated = hmac_output[0:16]"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Wire Format")
      (code "Packet = [HMAC(16 bytes)] + [GUID(6 bytes)] + [Payload(variable)]"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Implementation Requirements")
      (para "**Python:**")
      (code "import hmac
from cryptography.hazmat.primitives import hashes

def compute_hmac(data: bytes, key: bytes) -> bytes:
    \"\"\"Compute HMAC-SHA256, truncated to 16 bytes.\"\"\"
    h = hmac.HMAC(key, hashes.SHA256())
    h.update(data)
    return h.finalize()[:16]")
      (para "**Swift:**")
      (code "import CryptoKit

func computeHMAC(data: Data, key: SymmetricKey) -> Data {
    let hmac = HMAC<SHA256>.authenticationCode(for: data, using: key)
    return Data(hmac.prefix(16))  // Truncate to 16 bytes
}"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Validation Requirements")
      (para "**Constant-Time Comparison (CRITICAL):**")
      (para "All implementations MUST use constant-time comparison to prevent timing attacks.")
      (para "**Python:**")
      (code "import hmac

def validate_hmac(received: bytes, expected: bytes) -> bool:
    \"\"\"Constant-time HMAC comparison.\"\"\"
    return hmac.compare_digest(received, expected)")
      (para "**Swift:**")
      (code "func validateHMAC(received: Data, expected: Data) -> Bool {
    // CryptoKit provides constant-time comparison
    return received == expected  // Uses constant-time internally
}")
      (para "**Why constant-time matters:** Variable-time comparison leaks information about which bytes match, enabling timing attacks to recover the key."))
    (subsection
      (heading "Failed HMAC Forensics")
      (para "When HMAC validation fails, implementations MUST log to `/tmp/hmac_failures.log` for debugging:")
      (para "**Log Format:**")
      (code "[2026-01-18 15:42:13.456789] HMAC VALIDATION FAILED
Source: 192.168.1.100:54321
GUID: E32E3CA702DE
Expected HMAC: A1B2C3D4E5F6A7B8C1D2E3F4A5B6C7D8
Received HMAC: A1B2C3D4E5F6A7B8FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
Packet (hex): <full packet hex dump>
---")
      (para "**Properties:**")
      (item "Timestamp with microseconds")
      (item "Source IP and port")
      (item "Sender GUID (hex)")
      (item "Expected vs. received HMAC (hex)")
      (item "Full packet hex for offline analysis")
      (item "Append-only (do not truncate)")
      (para "**Security Note:** Log file does NOT contain keys. Safe to share for debugging."))
    (subsection
      (heading "Security Properties")
      (para "**Guarantees:**")
      (item "✅ Packet integrity (cannot modify without detection)")
      (item "✅ Packet authenticity (requires key to generate valid HMAC)")
      (item "✅ Constant-time validation (prevents timing attacks)")
      (para "**Does NOT Guarantee:**")
      (item "❌ Confidentiality (payload visible in plaintext)")
      (item "❌ Replay protection (same packet can be replayed)")
      (item "❌ Forward secrecy (key compromise affects all messages)")))
  (section
    (heading "Layer 2: Replay Protection")
    (subsection
      (heading "Purpose")
      (para "Prevent replay attacks where attacker captures valid packets and retransmits them."))
    (subsection
      (heading "Algorithm")
      (para "Nonce cache with time-based expiry."))
    (subsection
      (heading "Nonce Selection")
      (para "**Nonce = First 16 bytes of packet (HMAC value)**")
      (para "**Why HMAC as nonce:**")
      (item "Already computed for integrity check")
      (item "Guaranteed unique per packet (different HMAC = different packet)")
      (item "No additional overhead")
      (item "Collision-resistant (SHA-256 properties)"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Data Structure")
      (para "**Python:**")
      (code "@dataclass
class ReplayProtection:
    _seen_nonces: Dict[bytes, float] = field(default_factory=dict)
    max_age: float = 300.0  # 5 minutes

    def check_and_record(self, nonce: bytes) -> bool:
        \"\"\"Returns True if allowed (new), False if replay (seen before).\"\"\"
        now = time.time()

        # Check if seen
        if nonce in self._seen_nonces:
            return False  # REPLAY DETECTED

        # Record new nonce
        self._seen_nonces[nonce] = now

        # Periodic cleanup (every 100 records)
        if len(self._seen_nonces) >= 100:
            self._cleanup(now)

        return True  # ALLOWED

    def _cleanup(self, now: float):
        \"\"\"Remove expired nonces.\"\"\"
        expired = [n for n, t in self._seen_nonces.items()
                   if now - t > self.max_age]
        for n in expired:
            del self._seen_nonces[n]")
      (para "**Swift:**")
      (code "actor ReplayProtection {
    private var seenNonces: [Data: Date] = [:]
    private let maxAge: TimeInterval = 300  // 5 minutes

    func checkAndRecord(nonce: Data) async -> Bool {
        let now = Date()

        // Check if seen
        if seenNonces[nonce] != nil {
            return false  // REPLAY DETECTED
        }

        // Record new nonce
        seenNonces[nonce] = now

        // Periodic cleanup
        if seenNonces.count >= 100 {
            cleanup(now: now)
        }

        return true  // ALLOWED
    }

    private func cleanup(now: Date) {
        seenNonces = seenNonces.filter { _, timestamp in
            now.timeIntervalSince(timestamp) <= maxAge
        }
    }
}"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Configuration")
      (table
        (row "Parameter" "Default" "Unit" "Description")
        (row "`max_age`" "300" "seconds" "How long to remember nonces")
        (row "`cleanup_threshold`" "100" "count" "Trigger cleanup after N entries"))
      (para "**Cross-Language Requirement:** Both Python and Swift MUST use identical defaults."))
    (subsection
      (heading "Memory Management")
      (para "**Bounded Memory:**")
      (item "Nonce cache size bounded by: `packet_rate * max_age`")
      (item "Example: 1000 packets/sec × 300 sec = 300,000 nonces max")
      (item "Each nonce: 16 bytes + 8 bytes timestamp = 24 bytes")
      (item "Max memory: 300,000 × 24 = 7.2 MB")
      (para "**Automatic Cleanup:**")
      (item "Triggered after every 100 new nonces")
      (item "Removes nonces older than `max_age`")
      (item "Prevents unbounded growth"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Security Properties")
      (para "**Guarantees:**")
      (item "✅ Prevents replay of same packet")
      (item "✅ Memory bounded by time window")
      (item "✅ Automatic cleanup (no manual management)")
      (para "**Does NOT Guarantee:**")
      (item "❌ Protection within 1ms window (timestamp granularity)")
      (item "❌ Protection from different source IP (nonce is per-packet, not per-sender)")
      (item "❌ Protection after `max_age` expires")
      (para "**Attack Vectors Mitigated:**")
      (item "Attacker captures valid packet → Replays later → BLOCKED (nonce seen)")
      (item "Attacker sends duplicate packets rapidly → BLOCKED (nonce cache)")
      (para "**Attack Vectors NOT Mitigated:**")
      (item "Attacker captures packet → Waits 6 minutes → Replays → ALLOWED (expired from cache)")
      (item "Attacker sends packet to different instance → ALLOWED (different nonce cache)"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Integration")
      (para "**Receive Path Position:**")
      (code "HMAC Validation (Layer 1)
    ↓
Replay Protection Check (Layer 2) ← YOU ARE HERE
    ↓
Rate Limiting (Layer 3)")
      (para "**Code Example (Python):**")
      (code "# After HMAC validation passes
nonce = packet.hmac  # First 16 bytes
if not replay_protection.check_and_record(nonce):
    logger.warning(f\"Replay detected: {nonce.hex()}\")
    return  # REJECT packet")))
  (section
    (heading "Layer 3: Rate Limiting")
    (subsection
      (heading "Purpose")
      (para "Prevent DoS attacks where single peer floods system with unlimited packets."))
    (subsection
      (heading "Algorithm")
      (para "Sliding window rate limiting per peer."))
    (subsection
      (heading "Data Structure")
      (para "**Python:**")
      (code "@dataclass
class RateLimiter:
    max_requests: int = 10000  # CRITICAL: Must be 10,000 (not 100!)
    window_seconds: float = 60.0
    trusted_guids: Set[str] = field(default_factory=set)
    _request_history: Dict[str, List[float]] = field(default_factory=dict)

    def check_rate_limit(self, peer_id: str, source_addr: tuple) -> bool:
        \"\"\"Returns True if allowed, False if rate limit exceeded.\"\"\"
        # Check trusted GUID whitelist first
        if peer_id in self.trusted_guids:
            return True  # BYPASS rate limiting

        now = time.time()

        # Get peer's request history
        if peer_id not in self._request_history:
            self._request_history[peer_id] = []

        history = self._request_history[peer_id]

        # Remove requests outside window
        cutoff = now - self.window_seconds
        history[:] = [t for t in history if t > cutoff]

        # Check if over limit
        if len(history) >= self.max_requests:
            logger.warning(
                f\"Rate limit exceeded for {peer_id} from {source_addr}: \"
                f\"{len(history)} requests in {self.window_seconds}s\"
            )
            return False  # REJECT

        # Record new request
        history.append(now)
        return True  # ALLOW")
      (para "**Swift:**")
      (code "actor RateLimiter {
    private let maxRequests: Int = 10000  // CRITICAL: Must be 10,000!
    private let windowSeconds: TimeInterval = 60.0
    private var requestHistory: [String: [Date]] = [:]

    func checkRateLimit(peerID: String, sourceAddr: String) async -> Bool {
        let now = Date()

        // Get peer's history
        var history = requestHistory[peerID] ?? []

        // Remove requests outside window
        let cutoff = now.addingTimeInterval(-windowSeconds)
        history = history.filter { $0 > cutoff }

        // Check if over limit
        if history.count >= maxRequests {
            print(\"Rate limit exceeded for \\(peerID): \\(history.count) requests\")
            return false  // REJECT
        }

        // Record new request
        history.append(now)
        requestHistory[peerID] = history

        return true  // ALLOW
    }
}"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Configuration")
      (table
        (row "Parameter" "Default" "Unit" "Description")
        (row "`max_requests`" "10,000" "count" "Max requests per window")
        (row "`window_seconds`" "60.0" "seconds" "Sliding window duration")
        (row "`trusted_guids`" "empty set" "-" "GUIDs that bypass rate limiting")))
    (subsection
      (heading "Critical Historical Issue (SDTS Issue #2)")
      (para "**Problem:** Swift v1.0.2 had `max_requests = 100`, Python had `max_requests = 10000`.")
      (para "**Impact:** High-frequency trading systems blocked by Swift implementation.")
      (para "**Lesson:** Default values MUST match across ALL implementations.")
      (para "**Fix:** Changed Swift default to 10,000 to match Python.")
      (para "**Requirement:** ALL future implementations (Rust, Go, etc.) MUST use 10,000 req/60s."))
    (subsection
      (heading "Trusted GUID Whitelist")
      (para "**Purpose:** Allow specific peers to bypass rate limiting.")
      (para "**Use Case:** Trusted services in high-frequency trading environment.")
      (para "**Security:** GUID cannot be spoofed without key (HMAC validation ensures authenticity).")
      (para "**API:**")
      (code "rate_limiter.add_trusted_guid(\"E32E3CA702DE\")
rate_limiter.remove_trusted_guid(\"E32E3CA702DE\")
if rate_limiter.is_trusted(\"E32E3CA702DE\"):
    # Bypass rate limiting"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Memory Management")
      (para "**Bounded Memory:**")
      (item "History size per peer: `max_requests` timestamps")
      (item "Each timestamp: 8 bytes (float/double)")
      (item "Memory per peer: `10,000 × 8 = 80 KB`")
      (item "For 100 peers: `100 × 80 KB = 8 MB`")
      (para "**Automatic Cleanup:**")
      (item "Old timestamps removed on each check")
      (item "Sliding window ensures bounded size")
      (item "No manual cleanup needed"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Security Properties")
      (para "**Guarantees:**")
      (item "✅ Per-peer rate limiting (one bad peer doesn't affect others)")
      (item "✅ Sliding window (smooth rate enforcement, no burst windows)")
      (item "✅ Trusted GUID support (whitelist for services)")
      (item "✅ Memory bounded by peer count and window size")
      (para "**Does NOT Guarantee:**")
      (item "❌ Protection against Sybil attacks (attacker creates many GUIDs)")
      (item "❌ Protection against DDoS from many peers")
      (item "❌ Fairness (trusted GUIDs get unlimited access)")
      (para "**Attack Vectors Mitigated:**")
      (item "Single peer sends 100,000 packets/second → BLOCKED after 10,000 in 60s")
      (item "Single peer sends bursts → BLOCKED by sliding window")
      (para "**Attack Vectors NOT Mitigated:**")
      (item "Attacker uses 100 different GUIDs → Each gets 10,000 req/60s allowance")
      (item "Distributed attack from many legitimate peers → Each peer allowed"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Integration")
      (para "**Receive Path Position:**")
      (code "HMAC Validation (Layer 1)
    ↓
Replay Protection (Layer 2)
    ↓
Rate Limiting (Layer 3) ← YOU ARE HERE
    ↓
Application Delivery")
      (para "**Code Example (Python):**")
      (code "# After replay protection passes
peer_id = packet.guid.hex()
if not rate_limiter.check_rate_limit(peer_id, source_addr):
    return  # REJECT packet (rate limit exceeded)")))
  (section
    (heading "Layer 4: Encryption (Optional, Protocol 1 Only)")
    (subsection
      (heading "Purpose")
      (para "Provide payload confidentiality and authenticity for Protocol 1 messages."))
    (subsection
      (heading "Algorithm")
      (item "**Cipher:** AES-256-GCM (Galois/Counter Mode)")
      (item "**Key Size:** 32 bytes (256 bits)")
      (item "**Nonce Size:** 12 bytes (96 bits)")
      (item "**Tag Size:** 16 bytes (128 bits)"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Wire Format")
      (code "Encrypted Payload = [Nonce(12)] + [Ciphertext(variable)] + [Tag(16)]"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Key Management")
      (para "**Shared Key:**")
      (item "Same 32-byte key used for HMAC and AES")
      (item "Derived from shared secret or key exchange")
      (para "**Per-Peer Keys (Optional):**")
      (item "KeyStore allows different keys per peer")
      (item "Lookup by GUID")
      (item "Fallback to default key if peer not found"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Nonce Generation")
      (para "**Critical Requirement:** Nonce MUST be unique per encryption with same key.")
      (para "**Python:**")
      (code "import os

def generate_nonce() -> bytes:
    return os.urandom(12)  # Cryptographically secure random")
      (para "**Swift:**")
      (code "import CryptoKit

func generateNonce() -> Data {
    return AES.GCM.Nonce().data  // 12 bytes random
}")
      (para "**Why random nonces are safe:**")
      (item "96-bit nonce space = 2^96 possible nonces")
      (item "Birthday bound: ~2^48 messages before collision risk")
      (item "For typical workloads: Safe for trillions of messages"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Encryption")
      (para "**Python:**")
      (code "from cryptography.hazmat.primitives.ciphers.aead import AESGCM

def encrypt_aes_gcm(plaintext: bytes, key: bytes) -> Tuple[bytes, bytes]:
    aesgcm = AESGCM(key)  # 32-byte key
    nonce = os.urandom(12)
    ciphertext_with_tag = aesgcm.encrypt(nonce, plaintext, None)
    return nonce, ciphertext_with_tag")
      (para "**Swift:**")
      (code "import CryptoKit

func encryptAESGCM(plaintext: Data, key: SymmetricKey) throws -> Data {
    let nonce = AES.GCM.Nonce()
    let sealed = try AES.GCM.seal(plaintext, using: key, nonce: nonce)
    return nonce + sealed.ciphertext + sealed.tag
}"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Decryption")
      (para "**Python:**")
      (code "def decrypt_aes_gcm(nonce: bytes, ciphertext_with_tag: bytes, key: bytes) -> bytes:
    aesgcm = AESGCM(key)
    plaintext = aesgcm.decrypt(nonce, ciphertext_with_tag, None)
    return plaintext")
      (para "**Swift:**")
      (code "func decryptAESGCM(encrypted: Data, key: SymmetricKey) throws -> Data {
    let nonce = AES.GCM.Nonce(data: encrypted.prefix(12))
    let ciphertext = encrypted.dropFirst(12).dropLast(16)
    let tag = encrypted.suffix(16)

    let sealed = try AES.GCM.SealedBox(
        nonce: nonce,
        ciphertext: ciphertext,
        tag: tag
    )

    return try AES.GCM.open(sealed, using: key)
}"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Wire Format Compatibility (SDTS Issue #1)")
      (para "**Historical Note:** Initial implementation suspected Python/Swift incompatibility.")
      (para "**Reality:** Both use identical wire format: `[nonce(12)] + [ciphertext] + [tag(16)]`")
      (para "**Verification Method:** Dump actual bytes from both implementations, compare hex.")
      (para "**Lesson:** Always verify with real wire dumps before claiming bugs."))
    (subsection
      (heading "Security Properties")
      (para "**Guarantees (when enabled):**")
      (item "✅ Confidentiality (payload unreadable without key)")
      (item "✅ Authenticity (tag verifies payload not modified)")
      (item "✅ Integrity (tag detects any modification)")
      (para "**Does NOT Guarantee:**")
      (item "❌ Forward secrecy (key compromise decrypts all messages)")
      (item "❌ Traffic analysis protection (packet sizes/timing visible)")
      (item "❌ Metadata confidentiality (HMAC, GUID, headers visible)")))
  (section
    (heading "Per-Peer Key Management")
    (subsection
      (heading "Purpose")
      (para "Support multi-party scenarios where different peers use different keys."))
    (subsection
      (heading "Data Structure")
      (para "**Python:**")
      (code "@dataclass
class KeyStore:
    default_key: bytes  # 32 bytes, fallback key
    _peer_keys: Dict[str, bytes] = field(default_factory=dict)

    def get_key(self, peer_id: str) -> bytes:
        \"\"\"Get peer-specific key or default.\"\"\"
        return self._peer_keys.get(peer_id, self.default_key)

    def set_key(self, peer_id: str, key: bytes):
        \"\"\"Set peer-specific key (must be 32 bytes).\"\"\"
        if len(key) != 32:
            raise ValueError(\"Key must be exactly 32 bytes\")
        self._peer_keys[peer_id] = key")
      (para "**Swift:**")
      (code "actor KeyStore {
    private let defaultKey: SymmetricKey  // 32 bytes
    private var peerKeys: [String: SymmetricKey] = [:]

    func getKey(peerID: String) async -> SymmetricKey {
        return peerKeys[peerID] ?? defaultKey
    }

    func setKey(peerID: String, key: SymmetricKey) async {
        guard key.bitCount == 256 else {
            fatalError(\"Key must be 256 bits (32 bytes)\")
        }
        peerKeys[peerID] = key
    }
}"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Use Cases")
      (item "1. **Multi-Tenant Systems:** Different key per tenant")
      (item "2. **Peer-to-Peer Networks:** Different key per peer")
      (item "3. **Service Mesh:** Different key per service")
      (item "4. **Broadcast with Selective Access:** Default key for broadcast, per-peer keys for unicast"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Lookup Algorithm")
      (code "1. Extract GUID from packet
2. Convert GUID to hex string (peer_id)
3. Look up peer_id in KeyStore
4. If found: Use peer-specific key
5. If not found: Use default key
6. Validate HMAC with selected key")))
  (section
    (heading "Security Testing Requirements")
    (subsection
      (heading "Test Coverage")
      (para "All implementations MUST include tests for:")
      (item "1. **HMAC Validation**")
      (item "Valid HMAC passes")
      (item "Invalid HMAC rejected")
      (item "Modified payload rejected")
      (item "Constant-time comparison (timing analysis)")
      (item "2. **Replay Protection**")
      (item "First packet allowed")
      (item "Duplicate packet rejected")
      (item "Expired nonce allowed (after `max_age`)")
      (item "Cleanup removes old nonces")
      (item "3. **Rate Limiting**")
      (item "Under limit allowed")
      (item "Over limit rejected")
      (item "Sliding window behavior")
      (item "Trusted GUID bypass")
      (item "Per-peer isolation")
      (item "4. **Encryption (Protocol 1)**")
      (item "Encryption produces ciphertext ≠ plaintext")
      (item "Decryption recovers original plaintext")
      (item "Cross-language compatibility (Python ↔ Swift)")
      (item "Invalid tag rejected")
      (item "5. **Per-Peer Keys**")
      (item "Peer-specific key used when set")
      (item "Default key used when peer not found")
      (item "32-byte validation enforced"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Security Test Scenarios")
      (para "**Scenario 1: Replay Attack**")
      (code "1. Capture valid packet
2. Send packet again
3. Verify: Second transmission rejected")
      (para "**Scenario 2: DoS Attack**")
      (code "1. Send 10,001 packets from same peer
2. Verify: Packet 10,001 rejected (rate limit)")
      (para "**Scenario 3: Modified Payload**")
      (code "1. Build valid packet
2. Modify payload byte
3. Send modified packet
4. Verify: HMAC validation fails, packet rejected")
      (para "**Scenario 4: Encryption Confidentiality**")
      (code "1. Encrypt payload \"SECRET\"
2. Verify: Ciphertext does not contain \"SECRET\"
3. Decrypt ciphertext
4. Verify: Plaintext equals \"SECRET\"")))
  (section
    (heading "Threat Model")
    (subsection
      (heading "Assumptions")
      (para "**Trust Assumptions:**")
      (item "✅ Symmetric key is secret (not compromised)")
      (item "✅ Cryptographic algorithms are secure (SHA-256, AES-256-GCM)")
      (item "✅ RNG is cryptographically secure (os.urandom, SecRandomCopyBytes)")
      (item "✅ Implementation is correct (no bugs)")
      (para "**Network Assumptions:**")
      (item "❌ Network is hostile (attacker has full access)")
      (item "❌ Packets can be captured, modified, replayed")
      (item "❌ Timing information is observable"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Threats Mitigated")
      (table
        (row "Threat" "Mitigation" "Layer")
        (row "Modified packets" "HMAC validation" "Layer 1")
        (row "Spoofed packets" "HMAC validation" "Layer 1")
        (row "Replay attacks" "Replay protection" "Layer 2")
        (row "DoS from single peer" "Rate limiting" "Layer 3")
        (row "Eavesdropping" "AES encryption" "Layer 4")
        (row "Modified encrypted data" "GCM tag" "Layer 4")))
    (subsection
      (heading "Threats NOT Mitigated")
      (table
        (row "Threat" "Why Not Mitigated" "Possible Defense")
        (row "Key compromise" "Symmetric key system" "Use PKI (e.g., TaskHelloHandler)")
        (row "DDoS from many peers" "Per-peer rate limiting" "Network-level filtering")
        (row "Sybil attack (many GUIDs)" "No GUID authentication" "Require GUID registration")
        (row "Traffic analysis" "Metadata always visible" "Use mix networks, padding")
        (row "Timing attacks" "Constant-time comparison only" "Add jitter, padding")
        (row "Expired nonce replay" "Fixed time window" "Reduce `max_age` (trade-off)"))))
  (section
    (heading "Compliance and Standards")
    (subsection
      (heading "Cryptographic Standards")
      (item "**HMAC:** RFC 2104")
      (item "**SHA-256:** FIPS 180-4")
      (item "**AES-GCM:** NIST SP 800-38D")
      (item "**Key Sizes:** NIST recommendations (256-bit for AES, 256-bit for HMAC key)"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Best Practices")
      (para "✅ **DO:**")
      (item "Use constant-time comparison for HMAC validation")
      (item "Generate fresh random nonce for each AES encryption")
      (item "Use 32-byte keys for both HMAC and AES")
      (item "Log failed HMAC attempts for forensics")
      (item "Clean up expired nonces automatically")
      (item "Use sliding window for rate limiting")
      (para "❌ **DO NOT:**")
      (item "Reuse nonces with same key")
      (item "Use predictable nonces (counter, timestamp)")
      (item "Skip HMAC validation for \"trusted\" peers")
      (item "Disable replay protection in production")
      (item "Set rate limit to 100 (use 10,000)")
      (item "Implement custom crypto (use standard libraries)")))
  (section
    (heading "Implementation Checklist")
    (subsection
      (heading "Python Implementation")
      (item "[ ] HMAC computation using `hmac` module")
      (item "[ ] Constant-time comparison using `hmac.compare_digest()`")
      (item "[ ] Replay protection with dict-based nonce cache")
      (item "[ ] Rate limiter with per-peer history")
      (item "[ ] AES-256-GCM using `cryptography` library")
      (item "[ ] Per-peer key management with KeyStore")
      (item "[ ] Failed HMAC logging to `/tmp/hmac_failures.log`")
      (item "[ ] All security tests passing"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Swift Implementation")
      (item "[ ] HMAC computation using CryptoKit")
      (item "[ ] Constant-time comparison (CryptoKit default)")
      (item "[ ] Replay protection actor with nonce cache")
      (item "[ ] Rate limiter actor with per-peer history")
      (item "[ ] AES-256-GCM using CryptoKit")
      (item "[ ] Per-peer key management with KeyStore actor")
      (item "[ ] Failed HMAC logging to `/tmp/hmac_failures.log`")
      (item "[ ] All security tests passing"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Cross-Language Validation")
      (item "[ ] HMAC produces identical output (Python ↔ Swift)")
      (item "[ ] AES-256-GCM wire format compatible (Python ↔ Swift)")
      (item "[ ] Default values match exactly (10,000 req/60s, 300s expiry)")
      (item "[ ] Replay protection behavior identical")
      (item "[ ] Rate limiting behavior identical")
      (item "[ ] Interop tests pass (48/48)")))
  (section
    (heading "Version History")
    (item "**1.0.0** (2026-01-18): Initial specification"))
